
This illustrates optimizations with and without polarization.

xPOPTF executes a Fletcher-Powell optimization with polarization.
FlePow is normally used for complexes or flat energy surfaces;
BFGS is used when very near an energy minimum. 
The xPOPTF script performs two cycles of FlePow optimization. E.g.,
xPOPTF benwpi

