Currently, we feel that POLSCX = 1.0 is optimal and
it is used in the xPOPT and xPOPTF scripts. The chosen
polarizabilities are scaled linearly by POLSCX.

See JACS 117, 4177 (1995) for related experimental and
ab initio results.

If you wish to change the polarization scale factors, then
you need to change the last line of POPLSpar and POPLFpar
and use the command files POPTcmd and POPTFcmd. E.g.,
cp benKion.z optzmat
csh POPTFcmd >& log &

